= GL638 fixed-count confirmation
<gl638-fixed-count-confirmation>
The joint sampler did #strong[not] confirm a uniform gain over cut sampling. At 163,840 draws per method, composing Cut 1 LU-h focusing with the H/Z map reduced the imaginary-part empirical variance by 35.1%, but increased the real-part variance by 10.8%. Its real standard error is 5.2% worse and its imaginary standard error 19.4% better. The corresponding absolute-component variances show the same pattern. The preselected joint method remains the primary estimate; this result does not justify changing the winner after confirmation.

All 15 fresh runs completed with finite, stable results: five independent seeds (10007, 20011, 30013, 40009, 50021), 32,768 draws each, one iteration, 20 workers, 491,520 draws in total. The #link("GL638_MC_SCREEN.typ")[seven-method screen] fixed the three methods and the common score scales before these results. The interrupted #link("GL638_CONFIRMATION_ROOT.typ")[first attempt] contributes no samples to this table. All physical settings and channel cards remain fixed; `cuts_combined_joint` contains the six cut channels plus the composed Cut 1 LU-h → H/Z channel, without the optional soft LMB. It still includes the standalone Cut 1 sibling.

Means and pooled empirical standard errors below are in #strong[10⁻⁴ pb];. Maxima are absolute real/imaginary signed-component extrema in #strong[pb];, not a global maximum of the complex norm.

